{"answer": "395", "benchmark": "AssistantBench", "difficulty": "Medium", "explanation": "You need to find the visit cost (224) and the membership cost (130) on the different tabs, and then calculate the difference. The per visit cost is $30 per day x 4 adults is $120 per day for adults and the student cost per day is $14 so total daily cost is $120+14=$134 per day x 5 days= $670. We then compare that to the annual cost which is $250 per year for 4 adults (under the Keystone plan) and a student plan for the year is $25 so total cost is $250+$25= $275. So the difference in cost is $670 daily plans-$275 yearly plans= $395.", "gold_url": "https://philamuseum.org/visit/admission\nhttps://philamuseum.org/join/membership-levels-benefits", "id": "assistantbench:99da66d8af02491f98b98c56b26c709e773b5a2ad945fb280375951ba600de09", "source_id": "99da66d8af02491f98b98c56b26c709e773b5a2ad945fb280375951ba600de09"}
